[
    {
        "content": "<p>The equality <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ideal.card_inertia_eq_ramificationIdxIn#doc\">docs#Ideal.card_inertia_eq_ramificationIdxIn</a> between the cardinality of the inertia subgroup and the ramification index requires the extension of residue fields to be separable (in order for the cardinality of the automorphism group of residue fields to equal the degree).</p>\n<p>Currently <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ideal.card_inertia_eq_ramificationIdxIn#doc\">docs#Ideal.card_inertia_eq_ramificationIdxIn</a> requires <code>[PerfectField p.ResidueField]</code>, but in the review of <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41591\">#41591</a> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"488648\">@Xavier Roblot</span> and I have been discussing whether it might make sense to add a more specific typeclass such as</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HasSeparableResidueFieldsAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">isSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LiesOver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ResidueField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ResidueField</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and perhaps also</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HasSeparableResidueFields</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">isSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">under</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ResidueField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ResidueField</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Does something like this seem reasonable?</p>",
        "id": 616941100,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1786967317
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a way to make it work for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsLocalRing.ResidueField#doc\">docs#IsLocalRing.ResidueField</a> as well? Not prescribing an approach, but perhaps taking the residue field as a parameter and requiring isomorphism, or redefining the local ring residue field to be defeq to maximalIdeal.ResidueField?</p>",
        "id": 616941926,
        "sender_full_name": "Yakov Pechersky",
        "timestamp": 1786967624
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, if you applied <code>Algebra.HasSeparableResidueFieldsAt</code> to the maximal ideals of an extensions of local rings, then you would get a predicate on <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsLocalRing.ResidueField#doc\">docs#IsLocalRing.ResidueField</a>.</p>",
        "id": 616942329,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1786967776
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As for taking the residue field in as a parameter, I'm not so sure that's a good idea. I think the predicate should just refer to the rings, but then you could deduce separability for arbitrary choices of residue field as a consequence.</p>",
        "id": 616942557,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1786967850
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Good point! This assumption is also used in the comparison of two definitions of ramification index (index of valuation group vs index of inertia subgroup).</p>",
        "id": 617124551,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1787038416
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the fixed-<code>p</code> version <code>…At p</code> is probably what we want for <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41591\">#41591</a>, since the results there are about a fixed prime <code>p</code>. It would make things nicer in this PR for sure. </p>\n<p>On the design, I agree it is better to phrase it in terms of the rings. One small thing about the global version: since <code>⊥</code> is a prime ideal with <code>⊥.ResidueField = Frac B</code>, quantifying over all primes  would also require <code>Frac B / Frac A</code> to be separable, which is perhaps more than one wants in characteristic p. Maybe restricting to maximal ideals would avoid that.</p>",
        "id": 617403517,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1787132662
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't have a good sense of the correct global predicate in the non-Dedekind domain context, so maybe it would be better to just add the <code>At</code> version for now.</p>",
        "id": 617406125,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1787133363
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I prototyped the class and ran into something that I am not sure how to get around.</p>\n<p>This is the class I tried:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.HasSeparableResidueFieldsAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">p.IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">isSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P.IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P.LiesOver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>That part seems fine, and it works well with <code>Ring.HasFiniteQuotients</code> for a nonzero prime.</p>\n<p>The trouble is on the consumer side. For example, <code>card_stabilizer_eq_card_inertia_mul_finrank</code> needs <code>κ(P)/κ(p)</code> separable, where <code>κ</code> denotes <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ideal.ResidueField#doc\">docs#Ideal.ResidueField</a>, whereas the class gives separability for quotient rings. These two notions agree when <code>p</code> is maximal, and the corresponding instance exists, but for <code>p</code> prime, I could only find an <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/e076e1ca8f3970dfcc12618499a8acedf79bbd89/Mathlib/RingTheory/LocalRing/ResidueField/Instances.lean#L70-L71\">instance</a> providing <code>IsAlgebraic</code>. So I could use the class only after assuming <code>p</code> maximal, which loses the non-maximal primes the current lemmas cover.</p>\n<p>What seems to be missing is the separable analogue of that <code>IsAlgebraic</code> instance:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">q.LiesOver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">p.IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">q.IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime.IsLiesOverAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsIntegral</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p.ResidueField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q.ResidueField</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>coming from something like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsSeparable.of_isFractionRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsDomain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsDomain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsFractionRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsFractionRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsIntegral</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I did not find either in Mathlib, but I may well have missed them. Assuming both (with sorries proofs), the lemma does go through for a general prime with one extra line and an added <code>[Algebra.IsIntegral R S]</code>.</p>\n<p>Does that look like the right way to proceed, or is there something I'm missing?</p>",
        "id": 621005692,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1788353910
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why not ask for the residue fields to be separable rather than the quotients?</p>",
        "id": 621010788,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1788354855
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Something like this: (might require making <code>Localization.AtPrime.algebraOfLiesOver</code> into a local instance or something along those lines)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HasSeparableResidueFieldsAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">isSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LiesOver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ResidueField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ResidueField</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 621011006,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1788354897
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, this is definitely better. I have changed the class to your version and it works. Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 621044966,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1788360574
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, so here is what I have now, following your suggestion:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.HasSeparableResidueFieldsAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">p.IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">isSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P.IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P.LiesOver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime.IsLiesOverAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p.ResidueField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P.ResidueField</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Does that looks good to you?</p>\n<p>Note that making <code>Algebra κ(p) κ(P)</code> an instance instead does not work since it conflicts with the one coming from <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsLocalRing.ResidueField.algebra#doc\">docs#IsLocalRing.ResidueField.algebra</a></p>",
        "id": 621076266,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1788365682
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmmm, I don't really like having the quantification over <code>Algebra (Localization.AtPrime p) (Localization.AtPrime P)</code>. Is it possible to just use a single choice of the algebra in the definition, and then allow for arbitrary algebras in the API?</p>",
        "id": 621083132,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1788367069
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also note that <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Localization.AtPrime.IsLiesOverAlgebra#doc\">docs#Localization.AtPrime.IsLiesOverAlgebra</a> is going to get removed in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41100\">#41100</a></p>",
        "id": 621083190,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1788367081
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, so what about this definition then: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.HasSeparableResidueFieldsAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">p.IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">isSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P.IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P.LiesOver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime.algebraOfLiesOver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p.ResidueField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P.ResidueField</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P.IsPrime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P.LiesOver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">HasSeparableResidueFieldsAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Localization.AtPrime.IsLiesOverAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra.IsSeparable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p.ResidueField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P.ResidueField</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If I understand correctly this is what you had in mind. <br>\n(Thanks for the pointer to <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41100\">#41100</a>, I will switch to IsScalarTower once it is merged.)</p>",
        "id": 621275624,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1788419728
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, that looks great!</p>",
